{# Development mode. Deliberately the first card on the screen and styled by
   state: the expensive failure is not "we forgot to hide it" but "we launched
   six months ago and it was noindexed the whole time", and that one is only
   caught by making the state impossible to walk past. #}
<div class="card" style="border-color:{{ site.development ? 'rgba(245,158,11,.45)' : 'var(--border)' }}">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem">Development status
    <span class="badge {{ site.development ? 'warn' : 'ok' }}">{{ site.development ? 'In development' : 'Live' }}</span>
  </h2>
  {% if site.development %}
  <p class="mut" style="font-size:.9rem;margin:.2rem 0 .8rem">The door is shut three ways: <span class="mono">robots.txt</span> disallows every path, every page carries a <span class="mono">noindex, nofollow</span> meta tag, and an <span class="mono">X-Robots-Tag</span> header covers the PDFs and images a meta tag cannot reach. The site publishes, deploys and is shareable as normal; crawlers just stay out.</p>
  {# Kept as one quiet line rather than a warning block: development goes on
     while a site is being BUILT, before anything has indexed it, so the caveat
     is true but almost never the reader's situation. It still needs to exist
     for the day someone hides a site that was already live. #}
  <p class="mut" style="font-size:.82rem;margin:0 0 .8rem">Was this site already live and indexed? Blocking the crawl also stops Google re-reading it, so existing entries freeze rather than drop — to remove a site from search, leave it live until the results disappear, then switch this on.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="mut" style="font-size:.9rem;margin:.2rem 0 .8rem">This site is indexable. Search engines may crawl and rank every published page.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if can_manage %}
  <form method="post" action="/sites/{{ site.handle }}/settings/action">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrf }}"><input type="hidden" name="tab" value="{{ tab }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="action" value="development">
    <input type="hidden" name="development" value="{{ site.development ? '0' : '1' }}">
    <button class="button {{ site.development ? '' : 'ghost' }}" type="submit">{{ site.development ? 'Go live — allow indexing' : 'Switch back to development' }}</button>
    <span class="mut" style="font-size:.82rem;margin-left:.6rem">Saving republishes the whole site immediately.</span>
  </form>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{# Referenced-only publishing is the right default (page weight, and the CDN's
   file cap), but it is also the reason an image you just uploaded 404s at its
   own URL — and republishing never fixes that, because the build never copied
   the file. Given how unguessable that is from the outside, the card explains
   the mechanism rather than just naming the switch. #}
<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem">Media library
    <span class="badge {{ site.publishAllMedia ? 'ok' : '' }}">{{ site.publishAllMedia ? 'Whole library published' : 'Only what pages use' }}</span>
  </h2>
  {% if site.publishAllMedia %}
  <p class="mut" style="font-size:.9rem;margin:.2rem 0 .8rem">Every image, video and file in this site's library is published, so each one has a working public URL you can copy and use anywhere — an email, an ad, another site. Unused items count toward the site's file count, so trash what you no longer need.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="mut" style="font-size:.9rem;margin:.2rem 0 .8rem">Only media a page actually embeds is published. Anything else is left out of the live site, so <strong>its public URL returns 404</strong> — and publishing again will not change that, because the file is never copied. Turn this on if you want to link to library items directly.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if can_manage %}
  <form method="post" action="/sites/{{ site.handle }}/settings/action">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrf }}"><input type="hidden" name="tab" value="{{ tab }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="action" value="publish-all-media">
    <input type="hidden" name="publish_all_media" value="{{ site.publishAllMedia ? '0' : '1' }}">
    <button class="button {{ site.publishAllMedia ? 'ghost' : '' }}" type="submit">{{ site.publishAllMedia ? 'Publish only what pages use' : 'Publish the whole library' }}</button>
    <span class="mut" style="font-size:.82rem;margin-left:.6rem">Saving republishes the whole site immediately.</span>
  </form>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">Preview</h2>
  <p class="mut" style="font-size:.9rem">View the site in-browser with no deploy. Opening it checks whether anything changed since the last preview — if so it rebuilds (with a progress screen), otherwise it shows the current build straight away. Every internal path is relative, so it renders exactly as it will once published.</p>
  <a class="button" href="/sites/{{ site.handle }}/preview/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Preview ↗</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <details>
    <summary style="font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem">Authoring guide — how to design this site for 100/100/100/100</summary>
    <p class="mut" style="margin:.6rem 0 1rem;font-size:.88rem">Agents fetch the full guide via the MCP tool <span class="mono">get_authoring_guide</span> or <span class="mono">GET /api/v1/sites/{{ site.handle }}/authoring-guide</span>. Key rules:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Area</th><th>Rule</th><th>What to do</th></tr>
      {% for r in guide_rules %}
      <tr>
        <td class="mut">{{ r.category }}</td>
        <td>{{ r.title }}{% if r.ref %} <a href="{{ r.ref }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ref</a>{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="mut">{{ r.applies }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
  </details>
</div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Site details</h2>
      {% if can_manage %}
      <form method="post" action="/sites/{{ site.handle }}/settings/action">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrf }}"><input type="hidden" name="tab" value="{{ tab }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="action" value="site-save">
        <div class="row">
          <div><label>Name</label><input type="text" name="name" value="{{ site.name }}" required></div>
          <div class="tight"><label>Handle <span class="mut">(immutable)</span></label><input type="text" value="{{ site.handle }}" disabled></div>
        </div>
        <label>Base URL <span class="mut">(apex — a leading www. is stripped automatically)</span></label>
        <input type="url" name="base_url" value="{{ site.baseUrl }}" placeholder="https://example.com">
        <label style="margin-top:1rem">Serving <span class="mut">(how this site goes live — the Go-live card below walks through either path)</span></label>
        <div style="display:grid;gap:.5rem">
          <label style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start;margin:0;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--text)">
            <input type="radio" name="serve_mode" value="git" {{ site.serveMode == 'git' ? 'checked' }} style="margin-top:.25rem">
            <span><strong>Git → CDN</strong> <span class="mut">— every publish is pushed to the GitHub repo below; Cloudflare Pages / Netlify deploys it to their edge. Free, global, needs the repo + a one-time CDN hookup.</span></span>
          </label>
          <label style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start;margin:0;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--text)">
            <input type="radio" name="serve_mode" value="direct" {{ site.serveMode == 'direct' ? 'checked' }} style="margin-top:.25rem">
            <span><strong>Direct from this server</strong> <span class="mut">— the engine serves the built site itself on <span class="mono">{{ site.primaryDomain ?: 'the base URL domain' }}</span>. No repo or CDN account needed; publishes are live instantly. Requires the base URL and pointing the domain at this server.</span></span>
          </label>
          <label style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start;margin:0;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--text)">
            <input type="radio" name="serve_mode" value="ftp" {{ site.serveMode == 'ftp' ? 'checked' }} style="margin-top:.25rem">
            <span><strong>Your own web host (FTP/SFTP)</strong> <span class="mut">— every publish uploads the built site to hosting <em>you</em> control{% if site.ftpHost %}, currently <span class="mono">{{ site.ftpHost }}</span>{% endif %}. The site keeps running even if this server does not.
            {% if not site.ftpHost or not site.ftpUsername %}<strong>No target configured yet</strong> — use <em>Your own web host</em> under Go live below, which saves the connection and switches the site over in one step.{% endif %}</span></span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="row" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <div>
            <label>GitHub repo <span class="mut">(the dist repo the build is pushed to)</span></label>
            <input type="text" name="github_repo" value="{{ site.githubRepo }}" placeholder="git@github.com:you/site-dist.git">
          </div>
          <div class="tight"><label>Branch</label><input type="text" name="github_branch" value="{{ site.githubBranch }}" size="10"></div>
        </div>
        <label>Publish with <span class="mut">(a GitHub credential from your Account, or the server's global token — HTTPS repos only)</span></label>
        <select name="github_credential_id">
          <option value="">{{ global_token_configured ? '— global token —' : '— global token (not set on this server) —' }}</option>
          {% for c in github_creds %}<option value="{{ c.id }}" {{ site.githubCredentialId == c.id ? 'selected' }}>#{{ c.id }} {{ c.label }} ({{ c.email }})</option>{% endfor %}
        </select>
        {% if site.serveMode == 'git' and site.githubRepo %}
          {% if site.githubRepo starts with 'https://' and not site.githubCredentialId and not global_token_configured %}
            <p class="flash err" style="font-size:.85rem;margin:.5rem 0 0">Publishing will <strong>fail</strong>: this repo pushes over HTTPS, no credential is selected, and the server has no global <span class="mono">GITHUB_TOKEN</span>. Pick a credential above or add one on your <a href="/account">Account</a>.</p>
          {% elseif site.githubRepo starts with 'git@' and not deploy_key_exists %}
            <p class="flash err" style="font-size:.85rem;margin:.5rem 0 0">This repo pushes over <strong>SSH</strong>, where the credential above is not used — publishing needs a deploy key at <span class="mono">keys/{{ site.handle }}</span> on the data volume (none found). Use an <span class="mono">https://</span> repo URL with a credential instead, or add the key.</p>
          {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        <label>AI key <span class="mut">(OpenRouter key from an Account — powers translation fallback &amp; fact-checking)</span></label>
        <select name="ai_credential_id">
          <option value="">— none —</option>
          {% for c in ai_credentials %}<option value="{{ c.id }}" {{ site.aiCredentialId == c.id ? 'selected' }}>#{{ c.id }} {{ c.label }} ({{ c.email }})</option>{% endfor %}
        </select>
        <label>Team <span class="mut">(share this site with a team you belong to)</span></label>
        <select name="team_id">
          <option value="">— just me —</option>
          {% for t in user_teams %}<option value="{{ t.id }}" {{ site.teamId == t.id ? 'selected' }}>{{ t.name }}</option>{% endfor %}
        </select>
        <label>Workspace <span class="mut">(customer grouping — sites in a workspace only show when it is selected)</span></label>
        {% if site_workspace_accessible %}
          <select name="workspace_id">
            <option value="">— none —</option>
            {% for w in user_workspaces %}<option value="{{ w.id }}" {{ site.workspaceId == w.id ? 'selected' }}>{{ w.name }}</option>{% endfor %}
          </select>
        {% else %}
          <input type="hidden" name="workspace_id" value="{{ site.workspaceId }}">
          <p class="mut" style="font-size:.85rem;margin:.2rem 0 0">Assigned to a workspace by an administrator — only they can move it.</p>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="row">
          <div><label>Media public base <span class="mut">(R2 custom domain, optional)</span></label><input type="url" name="media_public_base" value="{{ site.mediaPublicBase }}" placeholder="https://media.example.com"></div>
          <div class="tight">
            <label>Status</label>
            <select name="status">
              {% for s in ['active', 'paused', 'archived'] %}
                <option value="{{ s }}" {{ site.status == s ? 'selected' }}>{{ s }}</option>
              {% endfor %}
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <label style="margin-top:1rem">Branding <span class="mut">(pick from the media library — images only)</span></label>
        {% if images|length %}
        <div class="row">
          {% set brandpickers = [
            {name: 'favicon_media_id', label: 'Favicon', sel: site.faviconMediaId, none: 'shell default'},
            {name: 'logo_header_media_id', label: 'Header logo', sel: site.logoHeaderMediaId, none: 'text name'},
            {name: 'logo_footer_media_id', label: 'Footer logo', sel: site.logoFooterMediaId, none: 'none'},
            {name: 'social_image_media_id', label: 'Social share image', sel: site.socialImageMediaId, none: 'none'}
          ] %}
          {% for p in brandpickers %}
          <div>
            <label class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem">{{ p.label }}</label>
            <div class="mediadrop" data-mediadrop>
              <input type="hidden" name="{{ p.name }}" value="{{ p.sel ?: '' }}">
              <button type="button" class="mediadrop-trigger"><span class="mediadrop-current"></span><span class="mediadrop-caret">▾</span></button>
              <div class="mediadrop-panel" hidden>
                <button type="button" class="mediadrop-opt" data-value="" data-thumb=""><span class="opt">∅</span>— {{ p.none }} —</button>
                {% for img in images %}
                <button type="button" class="mediadrop-opt" data-value="{{ img.id }}" data-thumb="/sites/{{ site.handle }}/media/{{ img.id }}/thumb">
                  <img class="opt" src="/sites/{{ site.handle }}/media/{{ img.id }}/thumb" alt="" loading="lazy" onerror="this.style.visibility='hidden'">#{{ img.id }} {{ img.original_name }}
                </button>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.5rem 0 0">The share image is the og:image / twitter:image used when a page is posted to Facebook, LinkedIn, X or Slack. The 1200&times;630 crop is generated automatically — pick any library image.</p>
        <script>
        (function(){
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-mediadrop]').forEach(function(root){
            if(root.dataset.mdInit) return; root.dataset.mdInit='1';
            var input = root.querySelector('input[type=hidden]');
            var trigger = root.querySelector('.mediadrop-trigger');
            var current = root.querySelector('.mediadrop-current');
            var panel = root.querySelector('.mediadrop-panel');
            var opts = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('.mediadrop-opt'));
            function paint(opt){
              current.innerHTML = '';
              var thumb = opt.getAttribute('data-thumb');
              if(thumb){ var im = document.createElement('img'); im.className='opt'; im.src=thumb; im.alt=''; im.onerror=function(){this.style.visibility='hidden'}; current.appendChild(im); }
              else { var sp = document.createElement('span'); sp.className='opt'; sp.textContent='∅'; current.appendChild(sp); }
              current.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' ' + opt.textContent.trim()));
            }
            function selectByValue(v){ var m = opts.filter(function(o){return o.getAttribute('data-value')===String(v);}); paint(m[0] || opts[0]); }
            selectByValue(input.value);
            trigger.addEventListener('click', function(e){ e.preventDefault(); panel.hidden = !panel.hidden; });
            opts.forEach(function(o){ o.addEventListener('click', function(e){ e.preventDefault(); input.value = o.getAttribute('data-value'); paint(o); panel.hidden = true; }); });
            document.addEventListener('click', function(e){ if(!root.contains(e.target)) panel.hidden = true; });
          });
        })();
        </script>
        {% else %}
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.85rem">Upload images in the <a href="/sites/{{ site.handle }}/media">Media</a> library to pick a favicon or logo.</p>
        {% endif %}
        {# Default meta description lives in the SEO card below.
           Canonical host (www ↔ non-www) lives in the Redirects card — it is
           the host-level counterpart of the path rules there. #}

        <label style="margin-top:1rem">ShortPixel API key <span class="mut">(optional — your own key + credits for image optimization)</span></label>
        <div class="row">
          <div><input type="password" name="shortpixel_key" autocomplete="off" placeholder="{{ site.shortpixelKeyEnc ? '•••••••• (saved — leave blank to keep)' : 'paste your ShortPixel key' }}"></div>
          {% if site.shortpixelKeyEnc %}<div class="tight" style="align-self:end"><label style="margin:0;font-size:.82rem"><input type="checkbox" name="shortpixel_clear" value="1"> remove</label></div>{% endif %}
        </div>
        {# Secrets are never re-displayed, so the field is always empty — say
           explicitly which key (site / engine-wide / none) is in effect. #}
        {% if site.shortpixelKeyEnc %}
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.3rem 0 0"><span style="color:var(--ok)">✓ Key saved for this site</span> — stored encrypted, never re-displayed. Leave the field blank to keep it; tick “remove” to drop it.</p>
        {% elseif engine_shortpixel_configured %}
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.3rem 0 0"><span style="color:var(--ok)">✓ Active via the engine-wide key</span> — no site key saved; images optimize through the server's <span class="mono">SHORTPIXEL_API_KEY</span>. Paste a key above to use this site's own credits instead.</p>
        {% else %}
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.3rem 0 0">No key configured — images are still optimized by sharp, just without ShortPixel's extra compression.</p>
        {% endif %}

        <label style="margin-top:1rem">Image compression <span class="mut">(drives ShortPixel's mode and the quality of the served AVIF/WebP/fallback variants)</span></label>
        <div class="row">
          <div>
            <select name="image_compression">
              <option value="lossy" {{ site.imageCompression == 'lossy' ? 'selected' }}>Lossy — smallest files (recommended)</option>
              <option value="glossy" {{ site.imageCompression == 'glossy' ? 'selected' }}>Glossy — visually lossless, a bit larger</option>
              <option value="lossless" {{ site.imageCompression == 'lossless' ? 'selected' }}>Lossless — pixel-faithful, largest files</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.3rem 0 0">Applies to new uploads and per-image optimizations. To re-encode images uploaded earlier at the new level, run <span class="mono">bin/fastsite media:regen {{ site.handle }}</span> (no ShortPixel credits used).</p>

        <label style="margin-top:1rem">Image sizes <span class="mut">(caps how large uploaded images are served)</span></label>
        <div class="row">
          <div><label class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem">Max image width (px)</label><input type="number" name="image_max_width" min="480" max="4096" step="1" value="{{ site.imageMaxWidth }}"></div>
          <div><label class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem">Logo width (px)</label><input type="number" name="logo_max_width" min="64" max="1024" step="1" value="{{ site.logoMaxWidth }}"></div>
        </div>
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.3rem 0 0">The largest responsive variant is capped at Max image width (a 4000px upload won't ship at 4000px). The header/footer logo is served at ~Logo width. Takes effect on the next upload; re-upload existing images to re-encode.</p>

        <label style="margin-top:1rem"><input type="checkbox" name="fact_check_enabled" value="1" {{ site.factCheckEnabled ? 'checked' }}> Enable AI fact-checking <span class="mut">(Perplexity-backed; on-demand from the content editor / API / MCP)</span></label>

        <label style="margin-top:1rem"><input type="checkbox" name="sanitize_content" value="1" {{ site.sanitizeContent ? 'checked' }}> Sanitize incoming content <span class="mut">(default)</span></label>
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.3rem 0 0">Uncheck only for a TRUSTED PORT: body HTML is then stored verbatim by default — inline styles, scripts, iframes and interactive markup are kept, the page is exempt from the zero-JS/PageSpeed audit, and translations keep it verbatim instead of stripping it back to plain markup. A single write can still override this with <code>sanitize</code>.</p>
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.83rem;margin:.9rem 0 0">
          Changing the repo resets the local clone so the next publish targets the new remote.
          Changing the name, base URL or branding republishes the site (canonical URLs, sitemap, llms.txt, the robots banner and the favicon/logo all embed them).
        </p>
        <p style="margin:1rem 0 0"><button class="button" type="submit">Save site settings</button></p>
      </form>
      {% else %}
        <dl class="kv">
          <dt>Name</dt><dd>{{ site.name }}</dd>
          <dt>Handle</dt><dd class="mono">{{ site.handle }}</dd>
          <dt>Base URL</dt><dd>{{ site.baseUrl ?: '—' }}</dd>
          <dt>Repo</dt><dd class="mono">{{ site.githubRepo ?: 'not set' }}</dd>
          <dt>Status</dt><dd>{{ site.status }}</dd>
          <dt>Search</dt><dd><span class="badge {{ site.development ? 'warn' : 'ok' }}">{{ site.development ? 'in development — noindex' : 'live — indexable' }}</span></dd>
        </dl>
        <p class="mut" style="font-size:.85rem">Only administrators or the site owner can change these.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {# Read-mostly panels collapse by default so the column is short on arrival;
       each still opens in place. Counts are in the summary so you can tell
       whether opening one is worth it without opening it. #}
    <div class="card">
      <details>
        <summary style="font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem">Components <span class="mut" style="font-weight:400">({{ components|length }})</span></summary>
        <table style="margin-top:.8rem">
          <tr><th>Handle</th><th>Type</th><th>Status</th></tr>
          {% for c in components %}
          <tr><td class="mono">{{ c.handle }}</td><td>{{ c.type }}</td><td><span class="badge {{ c.status }}">{{ c.status }}</span></td></tr>
          {% else %}
          <tr><td colspan="3" class="mut">None — upload via the API or MCP (<span class="mono">upsert_component</span>).</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </table>
      </details>
    </div>
